!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/validate-namespace.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/38/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/38/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  A namespace type declared with the kernel's `namespace` constructor: `headers` maps header names, an
  identifier family admitting `-`, to text. A namespace is a map in every fact, so a value of it is written and
  read as a map's is, keys judged by `key_type` and values by `value_type`.
  """
{
  header_name => !identifier_type { continue_add: "-" }
  headers     => !namespace { key_type: header_name  value_type: text }
  request     => { headers: headers }
}
